#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161693 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56c44f33-e6d3-5e34-9d9d-ded24576b82e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Conditional Expectations Given Joint and Marginal PDFs"}] :question/id #uuid "2eda20ae-ff4f-5c78-abaa-2c176968e908" :question/math-academy-id "e-10311" :question/problem "$f(x, y) = {y - x,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 \\le x \\le 0, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwisef_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{1}{2} + y,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\bigg\\begin{bmatrix}X \\,\\bigg & \\, Y=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\bigg\\end{bmatrix}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y = y \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x \\, f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) \\; \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y = y \\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$.\n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid y) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{Y}(y)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{y - x}{\\frac{1}{2} + y} \\\\\n&= (2(y - x))/(1 + 2y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq x \\leq 0, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nOutside this domain, we have\n\n$$\nf_{X \\mid Y} (x \\, \\mid \\, y) = 0\n$$\n\nNow, substituting\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the expression for $f_{X \\mid Y} (x \\, \\mid \\, y)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid \\frac{1}{2}) &= (2(\\frac{1}{2} - x))/(1 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - 2x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}xf_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid \\frac{1}{2})dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-1}^{0}x(\\frac{1}{2} - x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-1}^{0}(\\frac{x}{2} - x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{x^{2}}{4} - \\frac{x^{3}}{3}]_{-1}^{0} \\\\\n&= 0 - (\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161694 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162128 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea596df6-f52e-5347-afdd-78521b40525e" :knowledge-point/title "Conditional Expectation as a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3de4a4e5-824f-504b-ad7c-f088dd7569fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-10315" :question/problem "$f(x, y) = {\\frac{x + y}{4},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le x, 0 < x < 2 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwisef_{X}(x) = {\\frac{3x^{2}}{8},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x < 2 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=x\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ for $0 < x < 2$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X = x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\; \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X = x \\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$.\n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{X}(x)) \\\\\n&= ((\\frac{x + y}{4}))/((\\frac{3x^{2}}{8})) \\\\\n&= (2(x + y))/(3x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n0 \\leq y \\leq x,\\; 0 < x < 2\n$$\n\nOutside this domain, we have\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\mid X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x) = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}yf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{x}y \\cdot (2(x + y))/(3x^{2})dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3x^{2}}\\int_{0}^{x}(xy + y^{2})dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3x^{2}}[\\frac{xy^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{0}^{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3x^{2}}[\\frac{x^{3}}{2} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3} - 0] \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3x^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{5x^{3}}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3x^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{5x^{2} \\cdot x}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3x^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{5x^{2} \\cdot x}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5x}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161695 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "52bad65a-5481-5529-8e25-2763f57b755a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10316" :question/problem "${(3(1 + y^{2}))/(4),\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Find the conditional expected value $\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=1\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 1)$ is shown above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X = x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\; \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}yf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y \\cdot (3(1 + y^{2}))/(4)dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\\int_{0}^{1}(y + y^{3})dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}[\\frac{y^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{16}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcf85ec6-b20d-5540-a709-9ff28bc82ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation From a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983d667f-9351-5c43-8159-d56fc2c1baf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159705} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a66dcc-b0e1-5c5f-8805-7ece90dd1f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159706} {:answer/id #uuid "ba66cfd7-6641-5691-ac4e-8e5020696fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159707} {:answer/id #uuid "c866d6c5-1212-580c-bdd7-2206d8fe3fab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159708} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c21d5-588f-537b-ba3e-55ecf0a0ce93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159709}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8e99ef04-2d76-564c-b8d0-1708478bdb2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159704}] :question/id #uuid "9e557597-cc36-56e6-a5ea-6609d5dea4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-145631" :question/problem "$f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid 2) = {\\frac{x}{4},\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 3 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional expected value $E\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = 2\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid 2)$ is shown above."}]}
